bMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Redlich U, Hoeschen C, Doehring W. Assessment and optimisation of the image quality of chest-radiography systems. Radiat Prot Dosimetry. 2005;114:264–268. doi: 10.1093/rpd/nch559. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Tingberg A, Sjöström D. Optimisation of image plate radiography with respect to tube voltage. Radiat Prot Dosimetry. 2005;114:286–293. doi: 10.1093/rpd/nch536. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Deutsches Institut für Normung e.V. DIN 6868-13:2012-03: Sicherung der Bildqualität in röntgendiagnostischen Betrieben - Teil 13: Konstanzprüfung nach RöV bei Projektionsradiographie mit digitalen Bildempfänger-Systemen. https://www.beuth.de/de/norm/din-6868-13/145234631 . 2012. Accessed 09 Aug 2019. 20. Ewen K. Moderne Bildgebung. Stuttgart: Thieme; 1998. [ Google Scholar ] 21. Pötter-Lang S, Schalekamp S, Schaefer-Prokop C, Uffmann M. Detection of lung nodules. Der Radiologe. 2014;54:455–461. doi: 10.1007/s00117-013-2599-x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Monnier-Cholley L, Arrivé L, Porcel A, Shehata K, Dahan H, Urban T, et al. Characteristics of missed lung cancer on chest radiographs: a French experience. Eur Radiol. 2001;11:597–605. doi: 10.1007/s003300000595. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Widmer WR. Acquisition hardware for digital imaging. Vet Radiol Ultrasound. 2008;49:2–8. doi: 10.1111/j.1740-8261.2007.00326.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Norman G. Likert scales, levels of measurement and the “laws” of statistics. Adv Health Sci Educ Theory Pract. 2010;15:625–632. doi: 10.1007/s10459-010-9222-y. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Sund P, Bath M, Kheddache S, Mansson LG. Comparison of visual grading analysis and determination of detective quantum efficiency for evaluating system performance in digital chest radiography. Eur Radiol. 2004;14:48–58. doi: 10.1007/s00330-003-1971-z. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citation